result.description:
As our Chef, you will play a crucial role in maintaining and enhancing service standards while ensuring smooth daily operations. 
Your responsibilities will include:

· Cooking contemporary style dishes in accordance with the menu;
· Preparation of contemporary style dishes;
· Planning and development of menu in collaboration with Restaurant Managers;
· Ordering food and kitchen supplies;
· Discussing food preparation methods with kitchen staff, wait staff and managers;
· Demonstration and training of cooking techniques to employees;
· Involvement in the selection process of potential employees;
· Preservation of food;
· Compliance with occupational health and safety regulations;
· Staff rostering;
· Menu costing.
· Operational Oversight: Oversee restaurant operations, including scheduling, inventory management, and adherence to health and safety               regulations.
· Training and Development: Onboard new staff and provide ongoing training and development to existing team members.
· Quality Control: Monitor and improve the quality of food and service to ensure a consistently high standard.

Minimum Requirements:

· Education: Diploma in Kitchen Management and 1 year experience or related field, or 3 years of relevant experience in a similar role.
· Experience: Previous supervisory experience in a hospitality or restaurant setting.
· Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment, with excellent organizational and multitasking abilities.
· Knowledge: Familiarity with food safety and handling regulations.
· Passion: A genuine enthusiasm for the hospitality industry and a dedication to providing a remarkable dining experience.

Job Type: Full-time

Work Location: In person
